{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778779944,"nonce":"96V+mBseN2zSV3b9iH7dysbw9Dw=","title":"Run manifests as canonical lineage with database indexing","message":"## Problem\n\nFeedbax needs a durable way to represent run lineage and artifacts across Studio, scripts, CLI workflows, and downstream project packages. A database is useful for search and filtering, but making the database the only canonical source of truth makes runs harder to review, version, move between machines, reconstruct, or import from non-Studio workflows.\n\nThe design question is how to combine portable manifests with queryable database indexes.\n\n## Desired Direction\n\nUse manifest-first, database-indexed run lineage:\n\n- Manifest files are the canonical, portable, reviewable records of run identity and lineage.\n- The database indexes manifests and artifacts for fast search/filtering/query UI.\n- If the database is missing or stale, it can be rebuilt from manifests and artifact metadata.\n- If runs are created outside Studio, they can be imported by creating/reconstructing manifests and indexing them.\n\nA manifest should describe identity and lineage rather than storing large arrays: project, graph/spec references, training run sets, training runs, evaluation runs, analysis runs, reports, artifact paths, hashes, compatibility metadata, and parameter overrides.\n\nThe database should index flattened/queryable fields: run-set membership, run/eval/analysis type, artifact paths and hashes, flattened hyperparameters, protocol parameters, created timestamps, status, and lineage edges.\n\n## Design Questions\n\n- What is the minimum manifest schema for `TrainingRunSet`, `TrainingRun`, `EvaluationRun`, `AnalysisRun`, and report products?\n- Are manifests one file per object, one file per run set, or a hybrid?\n- How are parameter overrides represented relative to a base graph/task/loss spec?\n- How should database indexes represent flattened hyperparameters and JSON-path search?\n- How do we handle orphaned artifacts or reconstructed runs whose original manifest is missing?\n- Which parts belong in core Feedbax versus Studio-specific project state?\n\n## Related\n\n- `8d94424` — Feedbax design coordination.\n- `93f79f2` — Feedbax Studio design coordination.\n- `4e0d925` — Studio bottom pane should operate on pipeline collections.\n- `67bf476` — project-config-driven figure routing.\n- `0eebc71` — save_figure_with_spec reproducibility specs.\n- `f6a70cd` — EvaluationRecord setup metadata.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}